"props as story information"}, {"id": "eb1b520c-48d8-43a6-992e-96fd98be2058", "type": "concept", "title": "gesture and blocking"}, {"id": "d0176bf1-07da-486b-8873-5e1150344b34", "type": "concept", "title": "cinematic verbs"}], "description": "This subtopic trains writers to externalize inner life through behavior, objects, setting, and choice instead of relying on abstract exposition."}, {"id": "af1c2924-b08e-4a3c-8853-0ec57ac78232", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Writing for the reader and the viewer", "children": [{"id": "7cd345e0-8057-4f79-82dd-3b037fb29d22", "type": "concept", "title": "white space"}, {"id": "efa0d89f-2290-4c3e-b4a2-1bb502b08de8", "type": "concept", "title": "paragraph rhythm"}, {"id": "73d39441-b132-4374-ad89-951f6333c740", "type": "concept", "title": "lean description"}, {"id": "43082404-62e1-44d4-9bf5-25776c147302", "type": "concept", "title": "camera avoidance"}, {"id": "f5c7ebec-9a76-4c8b-a615-2e9f6449a7f8", "type": "concept", "title": "tone on the page"}, {"id": "f521c877-22e9-497d-a25c-abd070d9d1f2", "type": "concept", "title": "readability under time pressure"}], "description": "Students practice making pages move with enough detail for a professional reader and enough restraint for directors, actors, and designers to collaborate."}]}, {"id": "2f662886-f7e4-4780-a28a-39cc55453db8", "type": "topic", "title": "Story Concept, Premise, and Logline", "description": "A strong script begins with a focused dramatic idea. This unit develops the tools for testing whether an idea has conflict, stakes, audience promise, and enough pressure to sustain a film.", "children": [{"id": "08cfebdb-9cf6-4c40-916e-9fcdd43a4e0e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Premise and dramatic engine", "children": [{"id": "a6bd5af0-823c-4db6-b2e6-b1cee9cb3b22", "type": "concept", "title": "inciting situation"}, {"id": "376aa902-9a73-4390-9e0e-a78615ac723d", "type": "concept", "title": "dramatic engine"}, {"id": "2255167d-c6c9-4c3a-8f4b-f4b270cec0a3", "type": "concept", "title": "story arena"}, {"id": "c208d718-d4f9-4b5f-b3c9-129653e5f55e", "type": "concept", "title": "central contradiction"}, {"id": "091d6c08-7ab1-4f19-b2c4-54400b8a0407", "type": "concept", "title": "narrative pressure"}, {"id": "4cb9881a-7925-4fdd-aa74-9a338f947ba8", "type": "concept", "title": "story promise"}], "description": "Students learn to distinguish a topic from a story by identifying the force that keeps events moving and choices escalating."}, {"id": "833b0185-27e3-4ae0-beff-c23475ba9e75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Logline construction", "children": [{"id": "312c4d18-e5be-4fc7-94e6-58a40e4a77aa", "type": "concept", "title": "protagonist descriptor"}, {"id": "33eed7c6-8cbc-49a4-80aa-6eac69279d6f", "type": "concept", "title": "goal phrase"}, {"id": "0361b37f-b467-4417-961b-33cb049a5032", "type": "concept", "title": "antagonistic force"}, {"id": "46ec0df5-d0fd-4f17-b086-0a67dc711f82", "type": "concept", "title": "stakes clause"}, {"id": "b52dffe0-411a-454b-a7cc-368a471badae", "type": "concept", "title": "irony / hook"}, {"id": "3b0b7004-fa8e-449f-872b-3462e3b42693", "type": "concept", "title": "genre signal"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches the compact sentence that clarifies protagonist, goal, obstacle, stakes, and hook for workshop and industry contexts."}, {"id": "b791118e-f6be-44d0-8780-38b53b974900", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Testing and refining ideas", "children": [{"id": "20f20c2b-e23b-4c3e-9a43-3f13722cc4da", "type": "concept", "title": "what-if question"}, {"id": "c8c9cff6-dc21-487f-b24e-8303d993a39d", "type": "concept", "title": "conflict test"}, {"id": "f672dc1a-3d50-4439-87d4-2c548e7ad9ed", "type": "concept", "title": "stakes test"}, {"id": "72469451-09f2-4150-837a-5b0e827d214b", "type": "concept", "title": "freshness test"}, {"id": "caa10471-fadd-4122-9f47-6ea76aca93a2", "type": "concept", "title": "audience question"}, {"id": "10dc9d21-d3ea-4c90-b871-cbd556bbd795", "type": "concept", "title": "scope test for shorts"}], "description": "Students use quick diagnostics to find weak premises early and reshape them before drafting full scenes."}]}, {"id": "88728734-4257-4ef9-943b-4b6b50793ebd", "type": "topic", "title": "Character, Desire, Need, and Stakes", "description": "This unit builds characters who generate story through pursuit, contradiction, and change. Students connect external goals to internal needs without turning characters into abstractions.", "children": [{"id": "3c0e1747-f490-4371-8d01-f99222f10fe9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Want, need, flaw, and wound", "children": [{"id": "31ea07f7-c7a8-4d66-8510-1dc2b90d9eb3", "type": "concept", "title": "external want"}, {"id": "213a3e7b-d59b-4f7f-8b6a-3869576f53f1", "type": "concept", "title": "internal need"}, {"id": "6a8924d6-b8ce-4370-a26d-25de9dd05ecd", "type": "concept", "title": "character flaw"}, {"id": "1db04287-20b1-4ccc-930c-e6af99e757f9", "type": "concept", "title": "backstory wound"}, {"id": "aae7e79c-dace-464f-928d-288a1a781861", "type": "concept", "title": "misbelief"}, {"id": "b33dbec4-f664-42c9-856f-c844863d424d", "type": "concept", "title": "self-revelation"}], "description": "Students learn how visible goals and hidden needs create tension between what a character pursues and what the story ultimately confronts."}, {"id": "f8d1d450-9fc8-4162-b8e7-d4d7314fad22", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Character function and relationship design", "children": [{"id": "2de6238e-611d-4397-a564-03ac1505847a", "type": "concept", "title": "foil"}, {"id": "0c575e9c-e1d4-41f2-9c9d-685848b16e96", "type": "concept", "title": "mirror character"}, {"id": "26edab4e-19a5-47fc-9a27-412e980fcae5", "type": "concept", "title": "mentor"}, {"id": "97291945-db8d-47c5-aa87-dfbc30cdbaf7", "type": "concept", "title": "threshold guardian"}, {"id": "53d683bb-3530-4d37-8f49-cf46f76d48e3", "type": "concept", "title": "relationship arc"}, {"id": "adf7ccc7-87de-47f1-ba45-903db4421131", "type": "concept", "title": "ensemble balance"}], "description": "This subtopic maps how allies, antagonists, mentors, foils, and love interests pressure the protagonist from different angles."}, {"id": "3eccd3df-e269-4bda-9e46-9abb3f0399a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stakes and consequences", "children": [{"id": "02b2f719-eae0-49c2-922c-75e6ac1c0b49", "type": "concept", "title": "personal stakes"}, {"id": "1de481c0-4566-4d01-a331-e02817e9dfdb", "type": "concept", "title": "public stakes"}, {"id": "06ab4378-e1d3-493e-99c4-4438671ff0c8", "type": "concept", "title": "moral stakes"}, {"id": "9b9b3717-a568-449b-b31a-50a61a197e20", "type": "concept", "title": "emotional jeopardy"}, {"id": "de063eca-07b0-4e39-97b9-220f059c2850", "type": "concept", "title": "deadline pressure"}, {"id": "49e08d17-e464-4736-9fea-10f1575a5ec7", "type": "concept", "title": "irreversibility"}], "description": "Students learn to make choices matter by clarifying what can be lost, changed, exposed, or saved in every major turn."}]}, {"id": "63409268-0a89-4814-ac7b-d01cb3700a59", "type": "topic", "title": "Conflict, Obstacles, and Dramatic Escalation", "description": "Screen stories advance through resistance. This unit studies how obstacles, opposition, complications, and reversals transform a premise into a sequence of meaningful decisions.", "children": [{"id": "55d989c5-a0fc-4ee9-8848-eb3269c16fff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Types of conflict", "children": [{"id": "912fc617-f6b3-422a-bc48-8b45c387099a", "type": "concept", "title": "person versus self"}, {"id": "b143cd85-6063-4857-9ab8-77a8f925aa38", "type": "concept", "title": "person versus person"}, {"id": "66b5e61f-83ae-4ad6-89bf-67de7eb9d1af", "type": "concept", "title": "person versus system"}, {"id": "253adf85-0b5f-4240-a6c6-7b79fd1847a4", "type": "concept", "title": "person versus environment"}, {"id": "b707105b-c2bb-47b8-ad14-8e96e17a7c12", "type": "concept", "title": "moral dilemma"}, {"id": "55eccb46-8e02-4615-9d7d-4ae794c56221", "type": "concept", "title": "conflict layering"}], "description": "Students identify how internal, interpersonal, institutional, environmental, and moral conflict can operate together within the same scene or plotline."}, {"id": "d74cc381-f760-4d00-84c3-42250743f717", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Obstacles and tactics", "children": [{"id": "8d2032a1-811b-4860-a115-99ed2a58d178", "type": "concept", "title": "tactic"}, {"id": "5d64b63c-f176-414e-b51c-35f1605c4494", "type": "concept", "title": "counter-tactic"}, {"id": "54b7bc78-1c6f-4baa-bb2d-349656ab53c3", "type": "concept", "title": "blocking force"}, {"id": "4c1f9ec2-4882-473f-b638-d83ac3779067", "type": "concept", "title": "plan failure"}, {"id": "3a91dcfc-ff01-40ae-a4fa-50e9fda2ba1f", "type": "concept", "title": "adaptation"}, {"id": "465e1046-5c73-43ee-b1a4-1fc133b7cc26", "type": "concept", "title": "scene objective"}], "description": "This subtopic helps writers avoid passive protagonists by giving characters active tactics that shift when obstacles push back."}, {"id": "b32836db-8ce7-43a5-9738-16c546094379", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Escalation and reversals", "children": [{"id": "549c34f5-b3bc-44bc-975c-d67f6e754876", "type": "concept", "title": "reversal"}, {"id": "5baccaeb-d5c8-4466-a49d-f147fa1ac599", "type": "concept", "title": "complication"}, {"id": "f66abe4f-02b3-491f-92e8-35b1fda3097d", "type": "concept", "title": "raising stakes"}, {"id": "dfe81a47-d3a2-482f-ae16-533401d3c380", "type": "concept", "title": "point of no return"}, {"id": "b214d273-7f6b-41d9-b925-b439d3c5d3e4", "type": "concept", "title": "turning point"}, {"id": "9f7799ec-ec31-4492-bd21-88601f635600", "type": "concept", "title": "progressive difficulty"}], "description": "Students learn to increase pressure across scenes through surprise, cost, revelation, and the closing off of easy exits."}]}, {"id": "57c42881-dfa3-48f6-8b45-4d3b0d5ebd96", "type": "topic", "title": "Scene Construction and Beats", "description": "The scene is the basic dramatic unit of screenwriting. This unit teaches students to build scenes around intention, opposition, turn, and aftermath rather than simple information delivery.", "children": [{"id": "adbfb073-810a-4fae-9e65-9972bf019587", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scene objective and conflict", "children": [{"id": "a4281246-f0c6-4231-90aa-2b3ce77f2e3c", "type": "concept", "title": "scene want"}, {"id": "a8131826-db89-4666-a81c-2868dfb1b1e0", "type": "concept", "title": "opposition"}, {"id": "e5718c63-e9b2-43b8-89d1-a9afd40ff687", "type": "concept", "title": "urgency"}, {"id": "c8e7897d-5e5b-4035-8b6e-69d5de152c6e", "type": "concept", "title": "entrance value"}, {"id": "bfef3ac9-a658-405e-bd81-372ff6cb5b49", "type": "concept", "title": "exit value"}, {"id": "48b3c649-4520-4c21-89bb-1deace53769e", "type": "concept", "title": "dramatic question"}], "description": "Students learn to enter a scene knowing what each key character wants, why now, and what makes the exchange unstable."}, {"id": "a9ace23d-43c2-48af-b2f5-34f69cbc7eaa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Beat-by-beat movement", "children": [{"id": "144e7479-71a8-416f-8a28-e0504167d5dd", "type": "concept", "title": "beat"}, {"id": "b7dc0189-c266-4748-b1db-b25f3f57cd34", "type": "concept", "title": "turn"}, {"id": "2c3fc048-aad6-4723-8776-6d5551b30801", "type": "concept", "title": "status shift"}, {"id": "8df2aac4-ac73-4540-acbf-0cdee21ee0c4", "type": "concept", "title": "discovery"}, {"id": "8d7f77a8-0a69-4c25-bbd9-da72526d1a5d", "type": "concept", "title": "decision point"}, {"id": "8e636ec7-de67-4f95-b750-31b53d92b335", "type": "concept", "title": "button"}], "description": "This subtopic trains students to break scenes into turns so dialogue and action change direction instead of circling the same point."}, {"id": "be315c28-39af-4138-a91b-5a9a1216c2ed", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scene openings and endings", "children": [{"id": "392189b2-5309-4d11-9133-b80d6543e588", "type": "concept", "title": "late entry"}, {"id": "7168f366-e1fb-48a4-927a-98e2f4a6956a", "type": "concept", "title": "early exit"}, {"id": "90d463a7-588d-4023-b155-e98f6460224a", "type": "concept", "title": "scene hook"}, {"id": "408738c3-1b6e-456a-bb1d-56a74fc161e9", "type": "concept", "title": "cliffhanger"}, {"id": "0072fccd-494a-43b9-b744-2e1f8f78462b", "type": "concept", "title": "image button"}, {"id": "50d583c2-c63f-475a-8c75-fb8716627441", "type": "concept", "title": "transition logic"}], "description": "Students practice entering late, leaving early, and choosing final images or lines that propel the next scene."}]}, {"id": "e011a59b-f651-4120-aaa2-92cfd8b07471", "type": "topic", "title": "Structure: Acts, Sequences, and Turning Points", "description": "Structure is not a formula but a way of organizing pressure, expectation, and change. Students compare act structure with sequence thinking and short-film architecture.", "children": [{"id": "faedf9a5-6261-4dea-a212-26fd91afc5ec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Three-act architecture", "children": [{"id": "41b2f3c8-c7dd-4ac2-b5af-0a4f647e841d", "type": "concept", "title": "Act I setup"}, {"id": "16f08816-72b9-4706-9ac9-e1e0f0888827", "type": "concept", "title": "Act II complication"}, {"id": "50ad76ae-70cb-4346-828f-cd422aa8578b", "type": "concept", "title": "Act III resolution"}, {"id": "6ae45e50-6cc6-4abc-b9ef-d53af955e7f2", "type": "concept", "title": "inciting incident"}, {"id": "70c9fecb-a1cd-48ba-9ec4-719be82b1f29", "type": "concept", "title": "midpoint"}, {"id": "8f37ffe7-c103-49fb-bef8-67d6b754921d", "type": "concept", "title": "climax"}], "description": "Students study setup, confrontation, and resolution as flexible containers for dramatic change and audience orientation."}, {"id": "59212557-0353-4ee8-b12f-0ddb0cfea57d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sequence and beat-sheet models", "children": [{"id": "57c7b1b4-39f1-4988-bee9-f4a4065aec82", "type": "concept", "title": "eight-sequence model"}, {"id": "1ed42f0a-f511-4ab7-8e7a-14e5fd301c53", "type": "concept", "title": "Save the Cat beats"}, {"id": "689c8aa9-9518-49c8-b1a9-5f6e7c0a5c6c", "type": "concept", "title": "plot point"}, {"id": "5032ca2b-55a3-4701-ab6c-32fc3c698ec6", "type": "concept", "title": "pinch point"}, {"id": "bcd535f4-fbf7-47a4-a210-d8965ad5c07b", "type": "concept", "title": "false victory"}, {"id": "33f571e5-bdbb-4cc6-bf81-d1d0d9c44ae0", "type": "concept", "title": "all is lost"}], "description": "This subtopic compares practical outline systems so writers can choose tools that diagnose story movement rather than mechanically fill slots."}, {"id": "03aeeecd-109a-475d-abca-b6b81915f3c4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Short-film structure", "children": [{"id": "a9195140-fe12-4192-b66e-7254f2e14296", "type": "concept", "title": "single situation"}, {"id": "319bff28-ccae-4145-b72e-9ecf094177e4", "type": "concept", "title": "compressed arc"}, {"id": "e519c011-65a4-4b10-9a13-04ddee2f987d", "type": "concept", "title": "minimal exposition"}, {"id": "d4b8cc03-6188-430e-ade3-f49b9b7f7b38", "type": "concept", "title": "turnaround ending"}, {"id": "3dc4c966-7e73-4a31-b7de-2ed332f9a598", "type": "concept", "title": "visual payoff"}, {"id": "d7cc9620-949f-42ab-9872-100917b3260f", "type": "concept", "title": "festival short length"}], "description": "Students adapt structural principles to compressed stories where one decisive situation often carries the full arc."}]}, {"id": "fb62fa44-7393-49f7-86af-22cbd0a32b47", "type": "topic", "title": "Genre, Tone, and Audience Expectations", "description": "Genre gives writers a contract with the audience. This unit examines convention, variation, tonal control, and how genre expectations can guide or mislead viewers.", "children": [{"id": "de686e90-a935-4cfe-85aa-e87e8284533e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Genre conventions and promises", "children": [{"id": "3e155ccb-ee60-45df-9788-d33419cae5d0", "type": "concept", "title": "genre promise"}, {"id": "06f56bfe-b9cb-4452-b346-4d3b41637252", "type": "concept", "title": "iconography"}, {"id": "23b3d101-738f-4ae6-a78d-fa79a288f6b2", "type": "concept", "title": "set piece"}, {"id": "a8e46bd5-0d00-44c6-abb7-ea503fa1e5ef", "type": "concept", "title": "convention"}, {"id": "abfe8bdf-3fee-41a8-bd9e-1714f7833684", "type": "concept", "title": "trope"}, {"id": "1307f2da-8191-4806-879c-aa12dbe1935c", "type": "concept", "title": "obligatory scene"}], "description": "Students identify recurring situations, images, character roles, and emotional payoffs that shape audience expectation."}, {"id": "417c5c70-3901-466c-9bea-fd2bcd82cebc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tone and tonal consistency", "children": [{"id": "4d9526bb-0f4f-4d6e-9473-77c8b46246f1", "type": "concept", "title": "comic tone"}, {"id": "e2231577-f1ed-431e-97af-93cfd989148b", "type": "concept", "title": "dramatic tone"}, {"id": "caf9b7cf-6e1c-43e5-a855-9f13220436d4", "type": "concept", "title": "irony"}, {"id": "51c4285a-2f1a-4160-829c-9aeb77f3eee7", "type": "concept", "title": "dread"}, {"id": "d9c0e176-dcdf-4ddb-93ca-56dab19aa839", "type": "concept", "title": "sentimentality"}, {"id": "bb3121ac-8ce7-4a28-8b01-a4b2dd96c12b", "type": "concept", "title": "tonal rupture"}], "description": "This subtopic explores how page language, character behavior, pacing, stakes, and endings create the emotional temperature of a script."}, {"id": "06535293-efb2-4449-966f-474175ffd509", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Subverting expectations", "children": [{"id": "4932542d-5d6e-405d-a274-92d362ed2e41", "type": "concept", "title": "genre inversion"}, {"id": "9f173ae7-e1d7-455d-8613-89200fc186ef", "type": "concept", "title": "hybrid genre"}, {"id": "cc859582-5fb0-4626-8c52-44f6d69471d8", "type": "concept", "title": "anti-trope"}, {"id": "0544816d-9cb5-4582-bc61-fb25e702a0b9", "type": "concept", "title": "audience misdirection"}, {"id": "c6cf1801-5179-4574-8392-0513b2ed564c", "type": "concept", "title": "fresh angle"}, {"id": "c8412b5a-5240-4ef2-8360-d4e92cdab5b6", "type": "concept", "title": "ethical subversion"}], "description": "Students learn to revise inherited formulas by changing point of view, outcome, stakes, or character position without losing clarity."}]}, {"id": "3c28a143-9909-4f23-be7a-5aca65ed799a", "type": "topic", "title": "World, Setting, and Visual Specificity", "description": "Settings are active story tools, not neutral backdrops. This unit shows how place, era, objects, and social rules can reveal character and create constraints.", "children": [{"id": "fc272785-a0ff-48cd-8666-5d5a8e309011", "type": "subtopic", "title": "World rules and story arena", "children": [{"id": "994a6286-cdd5-4f4b-bb85-6bca8248eaa1", "type": "concept", "title": "story world"}, {"id": "3669a8e4-c72e-4fe6-8d80-1b00ffcb5edf", "type": "concept", "title": "arena"}, {"id": "0cb1625c-54e6-4681-a360-9655f69f1139", "type": "concept", "title": "rules of the world"}, {"id": "cd58edba-bd8b-4aa2-b804-3ab5fdc70d26", "type": "concept", "title": "social hierarchy"}, {"id": "d8e854b3-d188-4ea0-8934-440036f39555", "type": "concept", "title": "institutional pressure"}, {"id": "c9d2d4ad-88b7-40c8-bc3f-af35587d182f", "type": "concept", "title": "environmental constraint"}], "description": "Students define the practical, social, and emotional rules that make a script's world feel specific and usable."}, {"id": "2316810a-7cdc-4080-8fd6-f2e43bc9dad8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Location as drama", "children": [{"id": "57f129f1-9f25-485c-b35b-225cfc2a581e", "type": "concept", "title": "location pressure"}, {"id": "a56ad8f8-4819-488d-8bee-b021c49b34df", "type": "concept", "title": "blocking potential"}, {"id": "f68b94a0-7dd0-417a-ac00-d259da3d9316", "type": "concept", "title": "public versus private space"}, {"id": "45eb123c-b380-4888-a619-2ad4a1502ae9", "type": "concept", "title": "threshold"}, {"id": "48d7b931-047a-4ef7-8ca2-97fe84b27ddb", "type": "concept", "title": "revealing object"}, {"id": "9b350ec9-30ab-421f-853c-36f948f3a84d", "type": "concept", "title": "spatial irony"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches writers to choose spaces that sharpen conflict, block easy exits, and make character choices visible."}, {"id": "1db0020c-d45b-449a-ad2a-be8e185bca9c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual motifs and image systems", "children": [{"id": "86220a9d-6db2-4f52-8c9c-0b10156b3e2a", "type": "concept", "title": "motif"}, {"id": "53300de1-8748-4657-9446-4b3c46bdf866", "type": "concept", "title": "visual metaphor"}, {"id": "402e52d6-a01d-45af-86f6-c4a7ba2bd534", "type": "concept", "title": "recurring object"}, {"id": "11d451e0-6d04-4dba-a176-3064c93bb6d0", "type": "concept", "title": "contrast image"}, {"id": "0776840d-fc49-4a29-a867-49ca32d0e92d", "type": "concept", "title": "setup and payoff"}, {"id": "1251ee64-37e2-4198-82e0-da1c2354735a", "type": "concept", "title": "symbolic restraint"}], "description": "Students learn to use repeated images, colors, objects, and contrasts to support theme without explaining it directly."}]}, {"id": "3eb3b917-31be-4595-afdd-945c410676f4", "type": "topic", "title": "Dialogue, Subtext, and Voice", "description": "Dialogue should sound alive while doing dramatic work. This unit develops spoken language that reveals desire, conceals truth, creates rhythm, and distinguishes characters.", "children": [{"id": "b2a67cfe-3e9b-4037-96c9-5c0399e4df63", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dialogue as action", "children": [{"id": "3e832a23-d76f-4056-9079-1d394c04bdd5", "type": "concept", "title": "verbal tactic"}, {"id": "4ef25d4b-7e9c-4256-9adc-a967f5a55f15", "type": "concept", "title": "objective-driven line"}, {"id": "cd845114-f10d-4209-9b61-728c6ff1dab9", "type": "concept", "title": "deflection"}, {"id": "cb13665e-d2c2-4784-9a5f-0268c933ffc2", "type": "concept", "title": "threat"}, {"id": "2894f651-f2e3-4205-ae50-3b49853f5483", "type": "concept", "title": "seduction"}, {"id": "33d23a5b-7ea6-4cfe-9670-21c3c62d6409", "type": "concept", "title": "negotiation"}], "description": "Students treat lines as tactics characters use to get something, protect something, or change the terms of an exchange."}, {"id": "0713d2a0-f3e5-46ae-867d-467967c24972", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Subtext and silence", "children": [{"id": "b70ef0fc-bfad-44fc-99e5-748fc9ba705a", "type": "concept", "title": "subtext"}, {"id": "5d9b866b-b11c-44d5-a3c5-8b3d2ca9ecd3", "type": "concept", "title": "ellipsis"}, {"id": "05c76a51-3385-4fa6-8beb-3aea332f86d4", "type": "concept", "title": "loaded silence"}, {"id": "bf1c267e-e169-40c8-96e5-5c0fd0757b4b", "type": "concept", "title": "misdirection"}, {"id": "b22b6792-bca7-4c1b-9eda-4cae06557550", "type": "concept", "title": "double meaning"}, {"id": "ae9a02db-7f2f-43c1-91eb-899ce589b15b", "type": "concept", "title": "unsaid truth"}], "description": "This subtopic focuses on what characters do not say and how omissions, pauses, contradictions, and behavior carry emotional information."}, {"id": "f32c8acb-5b3a-49bd-ac09-b42430324a4c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Character voice and rhythm", "children": [{"id": "04d39d5c-12f3-4380-8a44-ca7df630e74b", "type": "concept", "title": "diction"}, {"id": "e222cbd1-dced-4fd4-8e8f-9b1646176518", "type": "concept", "title": "syntax"}, {"id": "e81b2618-ba6e-4eeb-8755-ec383724222a", "type": "concept", "title": "idiosyncrasy"}, {"id": "d7ca3b78-9caa-492e-95f7-4b2688ccd4dc", "type": "concept", "title": "status language"}, {"id": "27509ba3-e4c9-4a0e-b379-ace0424b4e35", "type": "concept", "title": "rhythmic contrast"}, {"id": "d87bfdd9-336b-435d-84f2-4f1a2d216419", "type": "concept", "title": "voice consistency"}], "description": "Students learn to distinguish voices through diction, syntax, pace, worldview, and relationship context instead of surface quirks."}]}, {"id": "30accfd7-bc1e-4eda-88cd-e55ec1dc3d36", "type": "topic", "title": "Theme, Point of View, and Meaning", "description": "This unit helps students connect story choices to larger questions without reducing scripts to messages. Theme emerges through conflict, consequence, pattern, and point of view.", "children": [{"id": "994be91f-ce0f-4607-8752-9f9c1f14dec8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Thematic question", "children": [{"id": "a9faf3e9-054d-4f69-bb05-29702bfc32f8", "type": "concept", "title": "thematic premise"}, {"id": "0068ca66-14f3-42af-b9bd-90944723eb1c", "type": "concept", "title": "central question"}, {"id": "bef7afe8-1dfa-4ae2-9d3d-edbf4cfd57b7", "type": "concept", "title": "moral argument"}, {"id": "feb3973a-168e-45a0-9c70-ba4073c77aad", "type": "concept", "title": "counterargument"}, {"id": "649feba5-616c-44f3-9f1b-915d786d29c5", "type": "concept", "title": "choice under pressure"}, {"id": "eb5cf675-d75a-44bb-be10-5c3913b3feea", "type": "concept", "title": "dramatic proof"}], "description": "Students frame theme as a living dramatic question that scenes test from multiple angles."}, {"id": "110a1933-9c61-4624-a30c-4b9c0169283b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Point of view and alignment", "children": [{"id": "ffa98ce1-abc7-4fb9-8af8-19beb126ea3b", "type": "concept", "title": "protagonist alignment"}, {"id": "9f6d0efb-f7d8-47c0-b26f-c891297250d0", "type": "concept", "title": "restricted knowledge"}, {"id": "0db729d2-3976-42b7-b241-a4e0f31633f0", "type": "concept", "title": "dramatic irony"}, {"id": "352bfb54-27ae-4f72-9d72-eb851a966e24", "type": "concept", "title": "subjective scene"}, {"id": "e7e7f4f4-4750-4095-a0ce-65e441c71b6d", "type": "concept", "title": "empathy strategy"}, {"id": "6fb65f6d-c686-412e-97d8-b7fc612c6f3d", "type": "concept", "title": "audience complicity"}], "description": "This subtopic examines how access to information, empathy, camera imagination, and scene selection position the audience."}, {"id": "17c00a23-fbf6-4894-be64-a14135294560", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Meaning through pattern", "children": [{"id": "0f4a3e4f-1b27-48ec-a7ba-1015ff06c067", "type": "concept", "title": "recurrence"}, {"id": "665c4f37-c6f1-4264-a63d-2d51c3ec7efd", "type": "concept", "title": "variation"}, {"id": "d11500c5-0bc0-4024-b140-7eb7820a2513", "type": "concept", "title": "echo scene"}, {"id": "69b284d4-4667-49fa-8947-aaafbe4cf927", "type": "concept", "title": "setup and payoff"}, {"id": "a1b31e74-20b9-40f7-bf7b-ffe1bf4bc616", "type": "concept", "title": "parallel action"}, {"id": "745dcd85-f477-4f36-9cd8-c061290e91b0", "type": "concept", "title": "final image"}], "description": "Students learn to revise repeated images, situations, and choices so the script accumulates meaning across its structure."}]}, {"id": "81621ce7-f99e-48ce-b37c-958fbb00a730", "type": "topic", "title": "Screenplay Format and Page Craft", "description": "Professional format is a reader courtesy and an industry standard. This unit covers technical screenplay conventions and the craft choices that make pages clean, quick, and filmable.", "children": [{"id": "712d1b9f-9f75-480f-aecd-27c7b3ac690f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Core format elements", "children": [{"id": "8e704228-93c9-49af-a39d-f1fda1839559", "type": "concept", "title": "scene heading"}, {"id": "915bd4ec-19ea-4bf0-ab78-ff7bda4d7055", "type": "concept", "title": "action line"}, {"id": "222f8ef8-6408-47c7-88e6-e92a772afdad", "type": "concept", "title": "character cue"}, {"id": "12d70028-8ab0-4b94-9ed5-8051f80feebd", "type": "concept", "title": "parenthetical"}, {"id": "ab281661-ffca-4788-9347-2a9c4e1f4827", "type": "concept", "title": "dialogue block"}, {"id": "3ce1eada-0c6c-4298-a0a0-677ec0b243ac", "type": "concept", "title": "transition"}], "description": "Students practice the fundamental building blocks of screenplay pages and learn when each convention is appropriate."}, {"id": "6ee22636-a547-4276-a25d-6b2db3e2290a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Formatting special cases", "children": [{"id": "0908a4c0-8aec-4556-9985-6a5d5e5d8d96", "type": "concept", "title": "intercut"}, {"id": "36c842cb-99af-4396-bff7-735e21f1a2ff", "type": "concept", "title": "montage"}, {"id": "e2f73101-0dd9-4474-a223-899ce6b0ab40", "type": "concept", "title": "series of shots"}, {"id": "0a73def9-9f5d-4bd4-b8e1-61a0bd78d9ce", "type": "concept", "title": "voice-over"}, {"id": "767c2a31-53ea-440f-ab1c-389a5351c299", "type": "concept", "title": "off-screen dialogue"}, {"id": "bc62f760-f891-466d-a8a9-8b916d991f43", "type": "concept", "title": "text on screen"}], "description": "This subtopic handles common technical situations that can confuse early drafts if not managed simply."}, {"id": "14774b7d-fc45-4223-8dba-4a6838bdd496", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Page-level polish", "children": [{"id": "b68d393f-dd75-42ac-a8e0-a77f4060ca5d", "type": "concept", "title": "widows and orphans"}, {"id": "428ec211-e7b8-4f9c-a3d1-2ef1061c262c", "type": "concept", "title": "dense action blocks"}, {"id": "6d281c8c-e2f4-432f-a530-f76df895c4f2", "type": "concept", "title": "active verbs"}, {"id": "66f8f683-d3a7-4004-8d32-74e83ca17a06", "type": "concept", "title": "line breaks"}, {"id": "3c45a64a-f1f5-4d51-a822-b9deec58de92", "type": "concept", "title": "page turns"}, {"id": "df05702c-29f1-4acb-a7a5-7ad88b834214", "type": "concept", "title": "proofreading standards"}], "description": "Students learn to diagnose overwritten pages, unclear geography, excessive camera directions, and rhythm problems before workshop."}]}, {"id": "5b6887c3-a537-4aac-8556-130ac72012fc", "type": "topic", "title": "Outlines, Beat Sheets, Treatments, and Pitches", "description": "Writers need intermediate documents that test story logic before drafting. This unit gives students practical tools for planning, presenting, and revising an idea.", "children": [{"id": "2112bb45-5cb9-4c2e-9bf9-06a1606b05b1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Beat sheets and scene lists", "children": [{"id": "d7fc6fec-fa77-408c-8453-175119516809", "type": "concept", "title": "beat sheet"}, {"id": "4552a38e-9b17-45ca-a76b-2f1ba8b295ab", "type": "concept", "title": "scene list"}, {"id": "63de82dc-e127-4262-aa76-9de65b5abf1d", "type": "concept", "title": "A-story"}, {"id": "e5fa690e-aa60-4e73-a808-d2f20e0a5fd4", "type": "concept", "title": "B-story"}, {"id": "5234e235-afd8-468c-a332-c21cc192b5cb", "type": "concept", "title": "sequence goal"}, {"id": "4d6d65ec-d745-4335-8e55-fa600f9405f0", "type": "concept", "title": "turn map"}], "description": "Students learn to map story movement in compact form so they can see cause, effect, escalation, and missing turns."}, {"id": "fe48c56e-aef7-43f4-b5f4-85fe5bfbe8f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Synopsis and treatment writing", "children": [{"id": "68833aef-231f-44b4-898d-fc08c9dee55a", "type": "concept", "title": "one-paragraph synopsis"}, {"id": "33c957bf-b34e-4c00-b892-480ff61f9ae6", "type": "concept", "title": "one-page synopsis"}, {"id": "359929fa-e9a8-456e-b4f1-05155b8f3a71", "type": "concept", "title": "treatment"}, {"id": "fdfa40a4-c460-4052-a1c1-b4a848b5e7ce", "type": "concept", "title": "present tense prose"}, {"id": "e6d22977-6dd2-4cb6-ada0-419d290e6c6c", "type": "concept", "title": "act summary"}, {"id": "84f44e27-9240-475c-9f8a-ae1f11838f70", "type": "concept", "title": "emotional spine"}], "description": "This subtopic converts a story into prose summaries of different lengths for workshop, development, and pitching."}, {"id": "b973edf8-2b1b-42aa-942c-b7978ff57962", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pitching the short script", "children": [{"id": "26e83202-7a90-4fe9-a689-9fcc573c7e5e", "type": "concept", "title": "elevator pitch"}, {"id": "5b5b02f7-94c7-4436-8d7e-36a7fcb33d8d", "type": "concept", "title": "comparables"}, {"id": "b8401513-2759-42eb-b32c-13bfc74c3769", "type": "concept", "title": "look and feel"}, {"id": "99dd26ad-3597-4b44-b33c-741404d516af", "type": "concept", "title": "why now"}, {"id": "5f7e83d0-007b-4fad-a5d7-ef135718c6d8", "type": "concept", "title": "target audience"}, {"id": "c8012ded-904c-4970-ab6e-ef508042a1d0", "type": "concept", "title": "production scope"}], "description": "Students practice verbal and written pitches that communicate premise, character, tone, and production feasibility."}]}, {"id": "b9e1943a-1915-48a4-b072-51a00fbe092d", "type": "topic", "title": "Workshop, Coverage, and Revision Practice", "description": "Revision is the core professional habit of screenwriting. This unit teaches students how to give useful notes, receive critique, diagnose drafts, and make intentional changes.", "children": [{"id": "7f9bf379-d29d-4cf4-9eef-02e998dd0131", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Workshop protocols", "children": [{"id": "1db39fc1-71f6-4280-aba5-2ed4c40200b1", "type": "concept", "title": "table read"}, {"id": "c59b8b45-eac9-43b8-9870-90f3951a0814", "type": "concept", "title": "clarifying question"}, {"id": "f3d6924d-ed3e-4fbe-a4db-3b0ddbb0c6cd", "type": "concept", "title": "reader response"}, {"id": "61f99f6e-6ee5-43ce-ab25-c9db03b4bf98", "type": "concept", "title": "note hierarchy"}, {"id": "6929fdd3-c6da-42b9-a756-6d47709224e7", "type": "concept", "title": "writer listening"}, {"id": "55767876-a23d-4dea-9da5-9d69fdd87a40", "type": "concept", "title": "critique etiquette"}], "description": "Students learn a shared vocabulary for discussing scripts generously, specifically, and rigorously."}, {"id": "58084b79-dca9-44e5-bd76-e033a1b55fb7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Script coverage and diagnostics", "children": [{"id": "bf232f02-719c-43c1-841e-5fdb33dbb2c2", "type": "concept", "title": "logline in coverage"}, {"id": "df2647cb-8006-40b8-b13b-3d8865f95b1c", "type": "concept", "title": "synopsis in coverage"}, {"id": "ac5b2021-bcbf-4ae5-a844-c0363f070381", "type": "concept", "title": "comments"}, {"id": "518fb37f-59b7-4201-8230-f2b542b2f69e", "type": "concept", "title": "consider / pass"}, {"id": "364b7c9c-e387-4b74-844a-9dee38d04dee", "type": "concept", "title": "character notes"}, {"id": "052f26f5-9766-456e-8458-93575a65c7c3", "type": "concept", "title": "structure notes"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces professional-style evaluation categories that help students see how readers assess story and craft."}, {"id": "598fbe44-7532-400a-a962-ec5161185788", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Revision strategies", "children": [{"id": "a686b39b-89f8-4b22-a862-e0c7d625668a", "type": "concept", "title": "revision plan"}, {"id": "ecbb92a1-f93a-408a-b3fc-599167c9e6ea", "type": "concept", "title": "page-one rewrite"}, {"id": "ecf5f514-1c59-49ce-a91e-ca0b772ff0a0", "type": "concept", "title": "scene rewrite"}, {"id": "b8027a63-b064-4536-bfaa-5385b231600e", "type": "concept", "title": "dialogue pass"}, {"id": "78102e35-ad27-4511-b8f8-82a051b0171e", "type": "concept", "title": "format pass"}, {"id": "d8bb9435-ccf8-4434-b601-e8c9671acf4c", "type": "concept", "title": "polish pass"}], "description": "Students practice moving from notes to action by prioritizing problems and choosing the right scale of rewrite."}]}, {"id": "f10ae925-aacf-4b9f-b93d-50af5ae6ba1b", "type": "topic", "title": "Short Film Screenplay Workshop", "description": "The course culminates in a complete short screenplay. Students apply concept, structure, character, scene craft, format, and revision to a script that can plausibly be produced.", "children": [{"id": "ab9dea53-36fd-4268-9ae2-373d066b0829", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Developing a producible short", "children": [{"id": "4b42eaf2-d57a-4205-bfc9-9aa09ea62085", "type": "concept", "title": "limited locations"}, {"id": "e54e3e3f-b4fb-4295-9528-66706322eaa6", "type": "concept", "title": "small cast"}, {"id": "5f5c6281-4c17-4fd0-976b-cd4e0be7be27", "type": "concept", "title": "clear conflict"}, {"id": "ae0f2536-4dff-4eff-9ef3-837f0376fd49", "type": "concept", "title": "visual premise"}, {"id": "666be238-5095-4266-8a61-2046ec278555", "type": "concept", "title": "short runtime"}, {"id": "1551cf47-fc6f-4cbf-8a3e-c96f43805fcd", "type": "concept", "title": "production constraint"}], "description": "Students learn to shape ideas around achievable scope while preserving emotional and cinematic ambition."}, {"id": "20a5a56a-9f79-42dc-a9c7-6675cdd19057", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Drafting and table reading", "children": [{"id": "783bd1d8-2967-4f35-b8ae-881cc34037fe", "type": "concept", "title": "first draft"}, {"id": "2a4e6403-bd96-4232-a0ec-70db3be89607", "type": "concept", "title": "cold read"}, {"id": "3885a4b3-30cd-4b84-b363-be05d6f3bc1a", "type": "concept", "title": "dialogue rhythm"}, {"id": "47501bfb-3d2d-4a37-a9e4-26c656afb1d3", "type": "concept", "title": "scene length"}, {"id": "fd7c2ba6-89cd-480d-9ad8-5e63fd676bad", "type": "concept", "title": "actor readability"}, {"id": "ee8345d1-1c61-4f8e-ab83-ae2dc647be51", "type": "concept", "title": "reader confusion"}], "description": "This subtopic moves students from outline to script pages, using performed reading to detect rhythm, confusion, and weak turns."}, {"id": "fd652e2c-7e92-4b87-87ca-2bfecc50cb6e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Final portfolio polish", "children": [{"id": "72a3e449-09c7-431c-9bd5-55b2a0e7005b", "type": "concept", "title": "title page"}, {"id": "64e53c8d-0b23-4117-a0fe-c9b08f2b3107", "type": "concept", "title": "final draft"}, {"id": "1382e60b-b69f-4cfd-9fbf-9ba793b41cc7", "type": "concept", "title": "submission formatting"}, {"id": "1f67b2c1-6959-47ac-ab8a-54bb96b1791e", "type": "concept", "title": "revision memo"}, {"id": "b4eb9c01-a27a-421b-a133-fd98111bc23e", "type": "concept", "title": "proofread"}, {"id": "94b646b9-6d49-474e-9ff9-e5a21dcad78e", "type": "concept", "title": "portfolio readiness"}], "description": "Students revise toward a clean submission-ready script package with title page, logline, synopsis, and reflective notes."}]}, {"id": "55e443f0-c7e3-4e2d-930b-ec99ac480207", "type": "topic", "title": "Ethics, Representation, and Authorship", "description": "Screenwriting instruction treats representation and authorship as craft questions as well as ethical ones. This unit helps students write with specificity, accountability, and imaginative range.", "children": [{"id": "54e095fd-9194-4e89-a3fa-9bfc43eb06bf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Writing across difference", "children": [{"id": "4303d736-1c00-42d7-a93c-78e905ad1587", "type": "concept", "title": "specificity"}, {"id": "9286a162-3241-4d98-a9a1-6591b4cc3e20", "type": "concept", "title": "stereotype audit"}, {"id": "3a3bf43f-46c0-45c8-82d1-9d454c4d3d6f", "type": "concept", "title": "cultural context"}, {"id": "dbb3c14c-3683-41ae-a5ae-5f8bf378534b", "type": "concept", "title": "consultation"}, {"id": "82d07fc4-ff25-40e3-96b6-acde0451eadc", "type": "concept", "title": "appropriation risk"}, {"id": "33222623-f4c0-4c80-99e4-fa4c63e2ab75", "type": "concept", "title": "character interiority"}], "description": "Students consider research, humility, collaboration, and limits when writing characters and communities outside their own experience."}, {"id": "3a9da18e-7d46-4974-b15b-34e9f265facd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Power, harm, and audience impact", "children": [{"id": "8997da97-fca7-46be-a464-0d7270f4a140", "type": "concept", "title": "framing"}, {"id": "5bc6983c-e5be-44be-a2d1-7643df125795", "type": "concept", "title": "normalization"}, {"id": "96e89e0f-03e8-432f-8d87-40ba6d0d2287", "type": "concept", "title": "punching down"}, {"id": "bf6541ef-a955-4740-9add-132943ade2ad", "type": "concept", "title": "trauma representation"}, {"id": "990d0a93-1b78-4744-b121-65b594391dec", "type": "concept", "title": "violence on page"}, {"id": "893b8079-69d4-431c-bddf-0fcbd1a41627", "type": "concept", "title": "consequence"}], "description": "This subtopic examines how scripts can reproduce or challenge harmful patterns through genre, point of view, humor, and consequence."}, {"id": "9e1ccd2a-4121-412d-b1e6-6f46f0514610", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Authorship and professional conduct", "children": [{"id": "788027d1-98a3-4b8f-82a8-4eeb93afada8", "type": "concept", "title": "copyright basics"}, {"id": "47d8e7a9-7dbb-4d63-9702-3c025a5d60c1", "type": "concept", "title": "collaboration agreement"}, {"id": "69b012af-9eb1-4179-903d-82cb8b4125bd", "type": "concept", "title": "credit"}, {"id": "2b38b198-05c9-4e83-bb3c-ac0956b92ef8", "type": "concept", "title": "plagiarism"}, {"id": "34c32165-e0ef-47b0-95ec-d6edad8a2742", "type": "concept", "title": "note boundaries"}, {"id": "590149c9-86af-4291-935c-e5e7797360d2", "type": "concept", "title": "professional email"}], "description": "Students learn basic norms of creative ownership, collaboration, feedback, and respectful workshop participation."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$scw1json$::jsonb,
